Someone put all the bits back together again.

00:12:06.020 --> 00:12:07.900
I say it was un-bombed. Erupted again.

00:12:07.900 --> 00:12:11.980
Oh! I'll give you the point for that. It was close to eruption.

00:12:11.980 --> 00:12:13.900
There was seismic activity.

00:12:13.900 --> 00:12:14.540
(Groans)

00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:15.620
# I'm on the cusp...

00:12:15.620 --> 00:12:17.060
It wasn't quite there.

00:12:17.060 --> 00:12:19.000
So what did Italy do?

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:22.720
Because it's obviously not Sicily anymore, it's the nation of Italy. What did they do...

00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:23.680
Surrendered!

00:12:25.960 --> 00:12:26.460
Italy.

00:12:26.720 --> 00:12:27.220
Italy.

00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:32.320
Went and parked up next to it, with a flag hung over the side of the boat, ready to go...

00:12:32.320 --> 00:12:34.280
Ooh. A little bit further than that.

00:12:34.280 --> 00:12:36.280
What? Actually stood on it as it was...

00:12:36.280 --> 00:12:37.960
Yeah, basically. Have a point. [ding]

00:12:37.960 --> 00:12:40.840
Actually, yeah, as it's going to be, erm...

00:12:40.840 --> 00:12:42.520
Yeah, it's going to be an extrusion, isn't it?

00:12:42.520 --> 00:12:46.200
So the actual bubbly material is at the bottom. It's just pushing up the dried column.

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:48.200
Dried! Cooled column.

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:50.760
Did they cap it so that it was above ground and then claim it?

00:12:50.760 --> 00:12:55.640
Chris, out of everyone was closest. They sent a diver down and put a flag, under water, on it.

00:12:55.640 --> 00:12:58.120
So then as, when it appeared...

00:12:59.480 --> 00:13:02.200
Italy. I respect that. That's pretty cool

00:13:02.200 --> 00:13:06.120
As the Scrapheap Challenge of boats comes round the corner of the Mediterranean

00:13:06.120 --> 00:13:08.120
Just an Italian, just waving.

00:13:08.120 --> 00:13:09.400
[frustrated cry]

00:13:09.400 --> 00:13:10.200
Right. Erm,

00:13:10.360 --> 00:13:11.480
Ah, by which point.

00:13:11.480 --> 00:13:14.880
can we get funding for this? Because that's just such a brilliant denouement.

00:13:14.880 --> 00:13:18.240
As the flag pops out. Just as it gets above.

00:13:18.280 --> 00:13:23.120
Just as they are about to start playing that really uppy downy Italian anthem that they've got.

00:13:23.480 --> 00:13:24.960
Out comes the Union Jack.

00:13:24.960 --> 00:13:27.480
[Cheering]

00:13:27.480 --> 00:13:29.800
The Italian one just flutters off.

00:13:29.800 --> 00:13:33.080
Sean Connery nods and drives away in his DB5 shaped boat.

00:13:34.840 --> 00:13:41.360
No, if Connery did it, just as the Union Jack came out, another one... a Scottish flag.

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:44.240
St Andrew's Cross.

00:13:44.240 --> 00:13:46.600
See, what they should have done is just laser carved it in to the rock.

00:13:46.600 --> 00:13:47.520
Hmmmm.

00:13:47.520 --> 00:13:48.120
Argue with that!

00:13:48.120 --> 00:13:51.200
But! Erosion was a problem already.

00:13:51.200 --> 00:13:53.280
As we have previously established.

00:13:53.280 --> 00:13:55.400
He's right you know.

00:13:55.400 --> 00:14:00.280
That have done stranger things, because they have all those bases out in the Pacific, haven't they, that are man made islands.

00:14:00.280 --> 00:14:02.640
They could just sail in there, put some hoardings round it.

00:14:02.640 --> 00:14:06.000
Pump the water out and start slapping concrete on this bastard, until it's actually big enough.

00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:10.280
Compared to reclaimed stuff in Japan...

00:14:10.280 --> 00:14:11.200
Do a Dubai on it.

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:12.040
Yeah!

00:14:12.040 --> 00:14:13.880
Do it in the shape of my face.

00:14:13.880 --> 00:14:16.680
Have like a nose shaped volcano in the middle of it.

00:14:16.680 --> 00:14:21.120
Well there's that one in Dubai, isn't there, where there's the guy's cut his name in canals.

00:14:21.120 --> 00:14:22.760
Hasn't he? That you can see from space.

00:14:22.760 --> 00:14:23.840
And then reverted it.

00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:25.680
They're not there any more.

00:14:25.720 --> 00:14:30.320
They're cut in, and then somehow they got... not paved over, but reclaimed.

00:14:30.320 --> 00:14:33.320
Because there's not much water out there, let's face it

00:14:33.320 --> 00:14:36.360
If the island does rise again, it's almost certainly going to be within...

00:14:36.360 --> 00:14:39.000
"THE ISLAND WILL RISE AGAIN!"

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:39.720
Thank you.

00:14:41.380 --> 00:14:45.880
If the island... appears above the waves again, because of modern treaties...

00:14:45.880 --> 00:14:47.720
Who will have rights to it now?

00:14:47.720 --> 00:14:49.060
Is it in international waters?

00:14:49.060 --> 00:14:50.100
No. Not any more.

00:14:50.100 --> 00:14:51.460
-- It's in territorial waters?
-- Yes.

00:14:51.460 --> 00:14:52.740
-- Is it Italian territorial waters?
-- There we go.

00:14:52.740 --> 00:14:54.600
-- It's Italy's.
-- Point. [ding]. Simple as that.

00:14:54.600 --> 00:14:58.220
"It's just a little island. We're not going to have a big fight over it."

00:14:58.220 --> 00:15:01.060
Those are words that will get spashed over a paper in about five years time.

00:15:01.060 --> 00:15:02.820
So they said 'It's yours'?

00:15:02.820 --> 00:15:05.880
I mean you could choose to interpret it as that.

00:15:05.880 --> 00:15:07.200
Ooh, so it's, who gets there first?

00:15:07.200 --> 00:15:08.400
To the scrapheap!

00:15:09.740 --> 00:15:11.520
At the end of the show, congratulations Chris.

00:15:11.520 --> 00:15:13.940
You win this week. I think fairly clearly

00:15:13.940 --> 00:15:16.080
Well I think Brannan put up a fight in the end.

00:15:16.080 --> 00:15:16.880
It was close, it was close.

00:15:16.880 --> 00:15:17.740
(It's mine.)

00:15:17.740 --> 00:15:19.800
Congratulations, you win a patch of Somerset marshland,

00:15:19.800 --> 00:15:21.240
that's been filled with oily fish,

00:15:21.240 --> 00:15:24.900
that was previously owned by a documentary film maker and a white rapper.

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:25.620
Oh God.

00:15:25.800 --> 00:15:26.300
Jesus.

00:15:26.640 --> 00:15:27.600
Go on. Come on.

00:15:27.860 --> 00:15:30.060
It's Michael Moore and Macklemore's mackerel moor.

00:15:31.760 --> 00:15:33.600
You enjoy your time on that.

00:15:33.600 --> 00:15:35.780
With that we say thank you to Chris Joel.

00:15:35.780 --> 00:15:36.560
Woohoo!

00:15:36.560 --> 00:15:37.520
Gary Brannan.

00:15:37.940 --> 00:15:38.480
Matt Gray.

00:15:38.480 --> 00:15:38.980
Bye!

00:15:38.980 --> 00:15:40.840
I've been Tom Scott, we'll see you next time.

00:15:42.340 --> 00:15:44.800
